    "text": "**Business & market dynamics:** The business returned to growth, with the core consumer tutoring segment showing sustained momentum and higher value capture per member, as average revenue per active member expanded sharply. Institutional revenue remains a smaller complement. Gross margin trends improved sequentially, signaling better unit economics. The company is pivoting fully toward an AI-native platform, which positions it to capitalize on evolving edtech demand, though the narrative is still anchored in a niche direct-to-consumer learning market rather than broad-based institutional adoption.\n\n**Management strategy and execution:** Leadership delivered on the three explicit goals set for the year: reigniting topline growth, advancing the AI-native platform transformation, and improving profitability. The team guided for full-year revenue and breakeven EBITDA in 2026 through disciplined cost management, lower sales and marketing spend, and operational leverage. This beat-and-raise cadence, coupled with a clear strategic pivot to an AI-first model, is strengthening management’s credibility with the market and framing NRDY as a disciplined turnaround story rather than a cash-burning growth experiment.",
